{"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart@navapbc.com","data":{"alias":"urban-dormant-boa","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Problem\n\nRealGitHost.commit_and_push clones the target repository with a bare `git clone <remote> <work>`. That pulls every branch and the full blob history even though the function needs exactly one ref. Against an established repository the transfer overruns the five-minute startToCloseTimeout the draft pull request workflow gives the commit activity.\n\nThe overrun is not recoverable. GithubMediator._gated advances the Postgres sequence gate before the effect runs and records the ledger entry only on success, so a timed-out commit leaves the gate advanced and every Temporal retry raises StaleActionError. The maximumAttempts of 3 is dead in this path.\n\n## Evidence\n\nMeasured inside the activity worker against the private remote with the injected token.\n\n- Full clone, 35 seconds, 1.1 GB\n- `--single-branch`, 40 seconds, 1.1 GB\n- `--filter=blob:none --single-branch`, 17 seconds, 239 MB\n\nBranch narrowing alone does not help because the repository is a single large pack. Omitting blobs is what cuts the transfer. Disk was not the constraint, 55 GB free.\n\nTwo massgov pilot runs failed this way. Worker logs show the clone at git_host.py:124 holding for the entire 300 second budget before cancellation. `_git` at git_host.py:84 runs subprocess with no timeout, so the thread outlives the activity and the clone keeps running after Temporal has given up.\n\n`ensure_branch`, directly above `commit_and_push` in the same class, already clones with `--branch --single-branch`. `commit_and_push` is the outlier.\n\n## Approach\n\nMove the existing `_ls_remote` branch probe above the clone so the ref to fetch is known before the transfer starts, then clone with `--filter=blob:none --single-branch --branch <branch-or-base>`.\n\nA blobless clone is safe here. The only history the function reads is commit messages, which it walks for the trailer idempotency check. It reads no blob. Blobs for the checkout are fetched on demand by the working tree materialisation.\n\nSeparately, raise the commit activity budget from 5 to 15 minutes through a single named constant used by both the commit and the CI repair call sites. The blobless clone cuts exposure roughly fourfold but does not bound the tail, and a timeout in this path is unrecoverable rather than merely slow.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- `commit_and_push` resolves the target branch before cloning and clones only that ref with blobs filtered out.\n- The trailer idempotency check still reads commit messages correctly against a blobless clone.\n- Both the commit and the CI repair activity use one shared timeout constant rather than two separate literals.\n- An integration test asserts the clone argument vector carries `--single-branch`, `--filter=blob:none`, and the resolved `--branch`.\n- No behaviour change to the push, the trailer, or the returned commit sha.\n\n## Out of scope\n\nThe sequence gate retry-masking defect itself. It is what makes this timeout fatal rather than slow, but fixing the gate ordering is a separate change with a much wider blast radius.","id":"f881-d2bf-c71e-440a","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["adevx","git-host","timeout"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"ADEVX-117 Narrow the commit clone to the single ref it needs"},"env_id":"8c3ef925-fbdc-4d88-8d59-f391cf59568c","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1789509509950907001,"uuid":"79acff2e-3ce6-4410-8b33-e142b6da2b37"}